Article30

(1) The Community shall be involved in the Protection of Women and Children. (2) Community involvement as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of participation through Prevention, services, empowerment, monitoring, supervision and fulfillment of the rights of Women and/or Children.

(3) The role of the Community in implementing the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by: a. providing communication and information through socialization and education regarding the rights of Women and Children;

b. providing suggestions and input in the formulation of policies related to the Protection of Women and Children;

c. reporting to the competent authorities if there is a violation of the rights of Women and Children;

d. playing an active role in the rehabilitation and social reintegration process for Women and Children;

e. forming family partners at the neighborhood/hamlet or village level by the Community;

f. establishing Women and Children Protection units within community organizations and educational institutions;

g. establishment and management of orphanages; h. establishment of Children rehabilitation centers;

i. provision of shelters and/or social;

j. job skills training; and

k. providing first aid when violations of the rights of Women and Children occur.

(4) Further provisions regarding Community participation shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 21

(1) The technical service institution as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (2) letter a is implemented by P2TP2A and FPK2PA.

(2) In the implementation of the Protection of Women and Children the Regional Government is obliged to establish a regional technical implementing unit for the Protection of Women and Children.

(3) The establishment of a regional technical implementing unit as referred to in paragraph (2) is stipulated by Regent Regulation after obtaining written approval from the Governor.

(4) In the case of the implementation of technical services as referred to in paragraph (1) the Regional Government may establish a task force. (5) The task force as referred to in paragraph (4) may also carry out institutional strengthening through cooperation and coordination with:

a. CFC task force;
b. CRA task force;
c. C/DRA task force;
d. schools and/ or educational institutions;
e. Children's forums;
f. children's centers;
g. community organizations;
h. Women's organizations; and
i. other institutions concerned with the fulfillment of rights and Protection of Children.
(6) The task force as referred to in paragraph (4) is a coordinative institution at the district and sub-district level that coordinates policies, programs and activities to realize sub-districts, child-friendly villages/wards.
(7) Further provisions regarding technical services as referred to in paragraph (3) are regulated by Regent Regulation.

